{"repositoryId":1411205418,"availability":"available","full":"abutlabs/the-gray-tutor","name":"the-gray-tutor","description":"Build a JAM client in TypeScript, one Gray Paper rule at a time.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T02:58:02Z","updated":"2026-10-16T19:08:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://abutlabs.github.io/the-gray-tutor/","topics":[],"demo":"https://abutlabs.github.io/the-gray-tutor/demo","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T19:09:40.853Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T19:09:40.853Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T19:09:40.853Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T19:09:40.853Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["How to use this project - Fork this repo and Build a JAM client in TypeScript.","The lessons explain the Gray Paper (version 0.8.0) and give the code in snippets. You assemble them into your own client in client/, run the tests at every step, and finish with a block importer that agrees byte for byte with the official test vectors. A scoreboard counts them as you go, every vector run whole, from 4 in lesson 2.6 to 1,406 of 1,428 at the end, and Grafana keeps the climb.","Building a JAM Prize implementation? This tutorial gives you a whole client's code, and some lessons show lasair's, another Prize entry. The Prize rules ask teams to build clean-room and to declare any implementation code they view: read the note on the Prize rules first."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abutlabs/the-gray-tutor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"319c2f9e2abbbbe7cb1175620b50317b44e3ed735d86d1ca53172ab6a6f10e5b","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T19:09:41.187Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T19:09:41.187Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"How to use this project - Fork this repo and Build a JAM client in TypeScript.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abutlabs/the-gray-tutor/blob/mai